# TypeScript Standards

## Strict Mode Requirements

```typescript
// ✅ ALWAYS use strict types
type Post = InferSelectModel<typeof posts>;

// ✅ ALWAYS explicit return types
async function getPost(): Promise<Post | null> { }

// ✅ Use readonly for immutable data
interface User {
  readonly id: string;
  readonly email: string;
  name: string; // mutable
}

// ❌ NEVER use any
const data: any = response; // FORBIDDEN
```

## Type Patterns

```typescript
// ✅ Const assertions for constants
const ROLES = ["admin", "user"] as const;
type Role = typeof ROLES[number];

// ✅ Use type inference where obvious
const count = 5; // inferred as number

// ✅ Prefer unions over enums
export const Status = {
  Active: "active",
  Inactive: "inactive",
} as const;

// ❌ Don't use enum
enum Status { Active, Inactive } // FORBIDDEN
```

## Type Inference Chain

```typescript
// Database → Drizzle → tRPC → React Query
import type { InferSelectModel } from "drizzle-orm";
type Post = InferSelectModel<typeof posts>;

export type RouterInputs = inferRouterInputs<AppRouter>;
export type RouterOutputs = inferRouterOutputs<AppRouter>;
```

## Avoid

- `any` type
- `enum` keyword
- Type assertions (`as`) without justification
- Null and undefined mixed
- `@ts-ignore` comments
